**Approach 2: WorkflowCore (Lightweight Alternative)**

DSL-based workflow definition:

```csharp
public class FloridaClaimWorkflow : IWorkflow<ClaimData>
{
    public string Id => "florida-claim-adjudication";
    public int Version => 1;

    public void Build(IWorkflowBuilder<ClaimData> builder)
    {
        builder
            .StartWith(context => ExecuteStep(context, "Receive Claim"))
            .Then<ValidateClaimData>()
            .If(data => data.IsHighValue)
                .Do(then => then
                    .StartWith<RequestSupervisorApproval>()
                    .WaitFor("approval", data => data.ClaimId.ToString())
                    .Output(data => data.ApprovalReceived, step => step.EventData)
                )
            .Then<ProcessClaim>()
            .If(data => data.RequiresPriorAuth)
                .Do(then => then
                    .StartWith<CheckPriorAuthorization>()
                )
            .Then<DeterminePayment>()
            .Then<SendEOB>();
    }
}
```

**Approach 3: State Machine for Simple Workflows**

For simpler sequential workflows, use state machine pattern:

```csharp
public class ProviderEnrollmentStateMachine
{
    private ProviderApplication _application;
    private ProviderEnrollmentState _currentState;

    public async Task<StateTransitionResult> TransitionAsync(ProviderEnrollmentEvent @event)
    {
        return _currentState switch
        {
            ProviderEnrollmentState.ApplicationReceived when @event == ProviderEnrollmentEvent.Validate
                => await ValidateAndTransitionAsync(),
            ProviderEnrollmentState.Validated when @event == ProviderEnrollmentEvent.BackgroundCheck
                => await BackgroundCheckAndTransitionAsync(),
            ProviderEnrollmentState.BackgroundCheckComplete when @event == ProviderEnrollmentEvent.Approve
                => await ApproveAndTransitionAsync(),
            _ => throw new InvalidStateTransitionException(_currentState, @event)
        };
    }
}
```

**Decision Matrix: Workflow Solution Selection**

```
Complexity | Human Tasks | Long-Running | Solution
-----------|-------------|--------------|----------
Simple (3-5 steps) | No | No | State Machine
Simple | Yes | No | Elsa Workflows
Moderate (6-15 steps) | No | No | WorkflowCore
Moderate | Yes | Yes | Elsa Workflows
Complex (15+ steps) | Yes | Yes | Elsa Workflows + Designer
Complex | No | No | Custom Code
```

